Subject: Serve org.gtk.Settings whatever GTK_USE_PORTAL says

GTK_USE_PORTAL=1 tells GTK 3 programs to use the portal file chooser and
print dialog; it says nothing about kded. GTK 3 on Wayland takes
gtk-modules only from the Modules property of org.gtk.Settings, so a
session that exports the variable gets no org.gtk.Settings, never loads
colorreload-gtk-module, and a running GTK 3 program does not repaint when
the colour scheme changes. Create the settings manager on every Wayland
session.

diff --git a/kded/gtkconfig.cpp b/kded/gtkconfig.cpp
index b1f7ad5..38a1f39 100644
--- a/kded/gtkconfig.cpp
+++ b/kded/gtkconfig.cpp
@@ -44,7 +44,9 @@ GtkConfig::GtkConfig(QObject *parent, const QVariantList &)
     dbus.registerService(QStringLiteral("org.kde.GtkConfig"));
     dbus.registerObject(QStringLiteral("/GtkConfig"), this, QDBusConnection::ExportScriptableSlots);
 
-    if (qgetenv("GTK_USE_PORTAL") != "1" && KWindowSystem::isPlatformWayland()) {
+    // GTK 3 on Wayland reads gtk-modules only from org.gtk.Settings, so without this service
+    // colorreload-gtk-module never loads and a running GTK 3 program keeps its old colours
+    if (KWindowSystem::isPlatformWayland()) {
         m_gsdXsettingsManager = new GSDXSettingsManager(this);
     }
 
